Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(frontend): snapshot upload sourceKind for result
 panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Context:
Owner source review of PR #144 HEAD 5bcaf753 found a blocking
state-semantics defect: UploadedPanel received live
editorState.editKind as sourceKind. pasteResponse persists after
upload, so switching Edit/File without a second upload could
reclassify the displayed result (File ?a → Text /d/<name>, or the
inverse). An in-flight tab change before the upload promise
resolved had the same race.

Expected behavior:
- Capture sourceKind once at upload start from the editor tab that
  initiated the upload.
- Bind UploadedPanel to uploadedSourceKind, not live editKind.
- pasteResponse, uploadedSourceKind, and uploadedEncryptionKey
  describe the same completed upload.
- Clear uploadedSourceKind when the displayed result is cleared
  (upload failure/abort or successful delete).

Acceptance criteria:
- File-tab foo.bin result keeps Download ?a and QR → ?a after
  switching to Text without another upload.
- Text-editor result stays Display-primary after switching to File
  without another upload.
- In-flight File upload still classifies as FILE if the editor
  switches to Text before the deferred POST resolves.
- Existing sourceKind contracts unchanged (MIME classification
  remains unused).

Constraints:
- Do not change storedMimeTypeForUpload() or PasteResponse schema.
- Do not change worker/storage product code.
- Do not revert to MIME classification.
- Do not export Patch 150 or merge into upstream-sync.

Validation:
- RED: three snapshot tests failed against live-editor derivation
- GREEN: pnpm exec vitest run frontend/test/index.spec.tsx -t
  "sourceKind snapshot" — 3 passed
- pnpm exec vitest run — 33 files / 262 tests PASS
- pnpm exec eslint frontend/pages/PasteBin.tsx
